From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: ahead read sync, a guest read of a fence-downloaded range waits for the frame that ran ahead (EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC)

DRAFT, not built. Our own work (guard-door job). Gated by EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC (exact 1), a
live switch (Id AheadReadSync, not armed); off by default. On: while the latest present returned
before its own frame's fence (EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1), every core forgets its kept read area at
that present, and a guest read of a Preflushable buffer range waits (up to 50 ms, 2 ms when a
channel is suspended) for that frame's bytes instead of taking guest memory as it is.
EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC_VERIFY=1 (boot) copies the bytes before the wait and counts what changed.
New file video_core/ahead_read_sync.h; RasterizerDownloadArea gains a defaulted `preflushed`.
10 s line while on: "EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC".

Reviewed draft (guard-door review, verdict "ready with corrections"): ahead-read-sync.v2.patch.
live_switch.h re-anchored after WritebackBands; all other +/- lines byte-identical to the v2.
